Have you ever seen Rugrats? Not at all appropraite for kids, totally
loaded with parental bonuses, presents radical modern concepts like
nudism (which isn't a big deal, it's just not appropriate for a kids'
show, and according to modern culture it's somewhat radical in
American culture), but it was one of the highest rated animations
during the 90's. I think having a fair balance is good, especially
since the type of people that would have their kids watch this would
appreciate it, and the types of kids that come from parents that would
show their kids this show would probably enjoy this kind of crap.

